1
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:05,940
It's my life.

2
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:06,917
It's your life.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,217
Fighting for tomorrow.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,080
Go get what you really want.
I want more. Any one more.

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,817
Come on, open up the door.

6
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,080
It's my life. It's your life.

7
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,600
Run like a winter fire.

8
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,880
I know you're strong.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,137
Believe you can achieve your goal.

10
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:23,377
Let's keep on going.

11
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,360
I'll not stay.

12
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,597
Let's do it again.

13
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,457
You know what I mean, baby!

14
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,037
No one can make it my dream come true?

15
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,240
Don't you feel it?

16
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:55,197
I really don't know what is
Something is testing me every day.

17
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,557
Hey, let's go.

18
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:57,470
Let's fly away.

19
00:00:57,553 --> 00:01:00,577
I know I never wanna come back here.

20
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,797
Hey, let's go.

21
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:05,677
Let's fly away the great
end of the unknown rules.

22
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,437
Standing up, blowing up.

23
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,617
My dream is getting wilder.

24
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,617
I'm not afraid, beat me, hit me.

25
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,137
I will never turn around.

26
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:17,917
Another day, another chance.

27
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,057
You know it's never too late.

28
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:23,560
If I can do it, so can you only without.

29
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,477
It's my life, it's your life.

30
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,577
Party for tomorrow, go
get what you really want.

31
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:35,680
I want more, anyone more,
come on, open up the door.

32
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,917
It's my life, it's your life.

33
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,957
Run like a wind, jump high, yeah, yeah.

34
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,637
I know you're strong.

35
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,057
Believe you can achieve your goal.

36
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,077
Let's keep on going, roaring.

37
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,357
It's my life, it's your life.

38
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:52,477
Fighting for your eyes that
I want, but your weary ones.

39
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:57,337
I want more, anyone more,
come on, open up the gate.

40
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:01,537
It's my life, it's your life,
shine like a star to be good.

41
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:06,257
I know you're strong, just that
you can't achieve your best.

42
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,640
Let's keep on going out of day.

43
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:19,020
You make my day every day.

44
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:38,280
Well, don't just stand there.

45
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,580
Stop me already.

46
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,440
Is all that fluttering wearing you down?

47
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:48,840
If you can't take it, why don't
you try groveling, toy soldier?

48
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,660
I thought so.

49
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,380
That confirms it.

50
00:02:55,580 --> 00:03:00,400
All those years ago, that toy soldier
crying like a baby in the rain.

51
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,600
That was the mighty Kiros.

52
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:11,620
Scarlet!

53
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,620
You're Scarlet's husband.

54
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:21,040
And Rebecca's father.

55
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,220
It's all connected.

56
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:29,050
Perfect!

57
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:34,200
Why, I imagine you've got quite a lot of
bad blood to settle with me, don't you?

58
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:35,740
That's correct!

59
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,100
Why do you think I came here?

60
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:43,280
Whoa, not bad!

61
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,297
It seems you found your footing.

62
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:47,860
But my cape's made of steel. Watch out!

63
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:53,370
Vyparaglase!

64
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:05,950
Mother!

65
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,040
Let me fight.

66
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,700
I won't get in your way.

67
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:12,740
Good call.

68
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:15,197
Wouldn't want to miss your own funeral.

69
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,220
Right, Rebecca?

70
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,860
I had such a lovely
time killing your wife.

71
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:25,080
I have to kill your daughter, too.

72
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:26,750
I'll fight alone.

73
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:27,974
I want to protect you.

74
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,920
This is my atonement.

75
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,100
For your mother.

76
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,580
And for forcing you to
fight alone all those years.

77
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:40,417
I'm so ashamed for
putting you through that.

78
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,180
For failing to protect you.

79
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:47,637
Now that my human form has returned,
I want my daughter to live in peace.

80
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:50,040
and never swing a sword again.

81
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,340
Uh-oh.

82
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:04,620
This is not good.

83
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,380
Lao-G is up for the count!

84
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,360
That's some real power.

85
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:21,853
I think I've heard of these guys before.

86
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,240
The Hapa Sui army from Kano.

87
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,220
I'll be careful.

88
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,960
Anyone can become an enemy at any time.

89
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,040
Hey, Gramps!

90
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,420
Come on, wake up!

91
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:34,440
Don't die! Not now!

92
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:38,507
I'll reserve two event venues
for us real soon, okay, sweetie?

93
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,920
Venues? For what?

94
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:43,004
One for our wedding, of course!

95
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,475
And then the funeral.

96
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,820
He's not dead!

97
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,220
Stand up, Gladius!

98
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:54,737
You don't want to die crawling on
the ground like a beast, do you?

99
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:55,650
Now fight!

100
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,200
Don't make me wait!

101
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:00,060
This should shut you up.

102
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:11,810
Gladius!

103
00:06:11,893 --> 00:06:12,760
Wait, you can't!

104
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,214
He's turned the whole area into a bomb.

105
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,760
You know what happens next.

106
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:27,119
You've been plotting this
for ages now, haven't you?

107
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:37,300
Hey, Bartolomeo!

108
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,257
Everything in the area is about to blow.

109
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:40,997
Let me inside your barrier, quick.

110
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,540
Not a chance. Why not?

111
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,777
If I open it, that'll put
me and Miss Robin in danger.

112
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,566
Also, enemies might sneak in.

113
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,737
But I'm your ally.

114
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:51,737
You can't just leave
me to die, gladius sir.

115
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:53,477
You're gonna blow us up too.

116
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,957
You'll be fine.

117
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,157
You're professionals after all.

118
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:58,517
Let me in.

119
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,437
Let me in.

120
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:02,860
Pop rock fest.

121
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,976
Farewell, Cavendish.

122
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:34,880
If you'd been stuck out there, that
would've wiped you out for sure.

123
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:38,870
Exactly!

124
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:41,057
So why'd you wait until the last second?

125
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:42,100
I could've died!

126
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:44,380
How about a thank you?

127
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,637
Is that any way to act towards
someone who just saved your life?

128
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,757
I've been out there
fighting all on my own.

129
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,680
Where's my thank you? Bite me!

130
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:53,990
That's enough.

131
00:07:54,073 --> 00:07:54,957
Let me out of here.

132
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,600
We need to win! Really?

133
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:00,257
You scream at me and beg to come
in and now you want out again?

134
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:03,017
Can't stick around for five
minutes just to be polite?

135
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,159
Show some manners!

136
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,640
It's not your house!

137
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:07,337
We're fighting a battle, okay?

138
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:08,420
Time for offense!

139
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,021
I'm not letting you in next time!

140
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,120
If I'm about to die, you'd better!

141
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,456
Do you want to win this fight or not?

142
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:19,170
Ugh!

143
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,852
We'll settle this later!

144
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:22,940
Crap, Miss Robin!

145
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:32,917
Okay, she's doing fine.

146
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,217
That's all that matters.

147
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:36,720
I'll be there soon, Rebecca. Stay safe.

148
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,600
You cunning little tramp.

149
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,700
How dare you?

150
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:45,517
You've caused the
executives enough trouble.

151
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,820
This ends now.

152
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,280
Catapult Pop!

153
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:56,770
Variability!

154
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,190
Back it!

155
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:06,860
Damn it!

156
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:08,317
I thought I'd blown him up!

157
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,282
Take it to the bank, Miss Robin!

158
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,740
I got you back!

159
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:15,133
Oh, Rooster, thank you!

160
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:17,360
I can't believe it.

161
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,940
She just winked at me.

162
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:23,840
Oh, yeah, that's the stuff.

163
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,647
She was totally like,
thanks, little rooster.

164
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,136
You can be my slave.

165
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:31,277
I'll even step on you
if you behave, right?

166
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,600
Okay, okay, sorry.

167
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:34,517
Gotta check yourself, Bato.

168
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,777
Keep that one in the realm of fantasy.

169
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,460
Anyway, dude, this is good stuff.

170
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,660
I'm hyped.

171
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,760
Huh? Cavendish?

172
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,537
You're behind the barrier, too?

173
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:50,444
Unfortunately for you, Gladius.

174
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:53,080
Blade of Beauty! Brachio!

175
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:54,580
Gladius, help!

176
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,360
Bottle of mayo?

177
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:08,820
Barrier balls!

178
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:13,277
It protects him when
it's crushing all of us!

179
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,197
Thanks, Miss Robin.

180
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:19,620
All it takes is one little wink, and
my heart lights up like an inferno!

181
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,117
Okay, Bartolomeo, that's enough!

182
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,857
You're gonna crush your ally!

183
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:33,237
Sorry, Cabbage, but there's a
good reason why I can't stop!

184
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,438
What might that be?

185
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:37,920
Cause I'm feeling super jazzed, baby!

186
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:39,740
Oh, that's lovely!

187
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,078
I'm high as a kite!

188
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:42,197
Can't stop this train!

189
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,515
WE 'LL HIT THE EMERGENCY BREAK, MORON!

190
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:45,480
NO CAN DO!

191
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:49,820
Dellinger! Hm?

192
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:51,770
Uh...

193
00:10:51,853 --> 00:10:53,877
Haven't you cleaned up
the second level yet?

194
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,060
Hey, Gladius!

195
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,221
Going for a jog?

196
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,186
I'll join you in a sec, okay?

197
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,588
Alright, but make it quick!

198
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,557
Nico Robin is climbing to the top,

199
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:06,197
and I can't stop her because my
hands are full with these two idiots!

200
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,700
Ah-ha! That's funny!

201
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,724
I can't wait to join the party!

202
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:14,339
I said ignore me at your own peril.

203
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:18,260
We're not finished yet.

204
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,997
You don't know how to
take a hint, do you, Mr.

205
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:21,910
Longarm?

206
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:28,277
So you've been hiding your extra joints
in those weird shoulder thingies.

207
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,125
That's kind of creepy, really.

208
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:35,177
I know you're a champion fighter, but
you've got a hole in your stomach.

209
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:36,760
Just drop dead already.

210
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,960
This is a man's world, and that
means I'm bound by a sense of duty.

211
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:44,580
To all those brave fighters
who fell before me.

212
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,100
How noble of you.

213
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:50,839
If you'd played dead, I
might have spared your life.

214
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,500
What is the point of standing up now, huh?

215
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:59,100
I can still buy time at least.

216
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:00,755
I hope that's enough.

217
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:04,620
All we have to do is keep
you busy until Straw Hat.

218
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:06,920
Bounce the tar out of Doflamingo.

219
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:09,180
So beat me if you like.

220
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:14,700
But the only victory that matters,
I'll win with my allies as a team.

221
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:21,886
So instead of calling it defeat,
you call it a noble sacrifice?

222
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:30,020
Spoken like a true loser, sense
of duty is a shackle for the weak.

223
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:33,157
Oh,

224
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:39,580
my God.

225
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:07,100
I'm no ordinary human, either.

226
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:13,140
The strength of a fighting fish
courses through every muscle.

227
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:33,400
I'm here, Gladius!

228
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:34,857
You still need my help?

229
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:35,960
Where'd you go?

230
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:42,760
Gladius, hello?

231
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,357
Dellinger, go back down.

232
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:46,852
It's too dangerous here.

233
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,820
There's a deadly enemy!

234
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:51,580
That doesn't sound like you.

235
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:53,497
Come on, I've seen the competition,

236
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:56,580
and if we team up, there's
nobody that can beat us.

237
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:06,780
Dillinger!

238
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,600
Dillinger!

239
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:26,310
Damn it.

240
00:14:26,393 --> 00:14:27,223
He's finished.

241
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:30,980
Whoa, jeez.

242
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:32,748
What is going on out there?

243
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:35,061
That little creep with the horns.

244
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:37,620
And all the soldiers totally ate it.

245
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,160
One dude did all of that.

246
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:45,500
Oh, man.

247
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:46,917
That guy's freaky as hell.

248
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,529
What is up with that face?

249
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,190
Wait.

250
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:55,500
Who is that?

251
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:59,337
He's dressed like cabbage,
but that can't be him.

252
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:01,300
I mean, can it?

253
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,320
Wait a sec.

254
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:18,617
Something just like this happened back
at the Coliseum during the D-Block fight.

255
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,380
I'm speechless, folks.

256
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:23,300
Just like that, the
whole ring is out cold.

257
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:36,695
He cleared out those gladiators
in the blink of an eye.

258
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:40,600
The clothes, the hair,
the sword, all Cavendish.

259
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:43,195
But that face is somebody else's dish.

260
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:45,986
So what kind of dish are
we dealing with here?

261
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:48,370
Huh?

262
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:52,160
That was too fast to even see.

263
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,600
Holy crap, this guy's scary.

264
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:56,677
Hey, creepy face, who are you?

265
00:15:56,760 --> 00:16:00,840
You can zip around as fast as you
like, but you're not getting in,

266
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,433
even if you ask nicely.

267
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:05,257
What do you want to kill me for anyway?

